{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01C5XaQFACF8DZ13xB1uua9Q","type":"tool_result","content":"# GEPA Hardware Requirements\n\nBased on the documentation provided, **GEPA does not require a local GPU** for the optimization loop itself.\n\nThe framework is designed to work with **API-only models**. As stated in the materials: *\"No weights access needed. Optimize GPT-5, Claude, Gemini directly through their APIs.\"*\n\nGEPA operates by:\n- Calling LLM APIs (task evaluation and reflection models)\n- Managing the evolutionary search algorithm locally\n- Processing execution traces and diagnostic feedback\n\nThe main computational requirement is network access to LLM providers rather than GPU hardware. This makes GEPA accessible to users without specialized computing infrastructure, though you'll need API keys and associated costs for the LLM service calls during optimization.\n\nThe typical optimization loop uses 100–500 evaluations, which scales based on your evaluation metric complexity rather than GPU availability."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"85c67b5e-349d-4078-9cba-9904b0f906d3","uuid":"07f1728a-dcca-4292-9538-25a39065add7","timestamp":"2026-07-29T01:25:34.828Z","tool_use_result":{"bytes":39867,"code":200,"codeText":"OK","result":"# GEPA Hardware Requirements\n\nBased on the documentation provided, **GEPA does not require a local GPU** for the optimization loop itself.\n\nThe framework is designed to work with **API-only models**. As stated in the materials: *\"No weights access needed. Optimize GPT-5, Claude, Gemini directly through their APIs.\"*\n\nGEPA operates by:\n- Calling LLM APIs (task evaluation and reflection models)\n- Managing the evolutionary search algorithm locally\n- Processing execution traces and diagnostic feedback\n\nThe main computational requirement is network access to LLM providers rather than GPU hardware. This makes GEPA accessible to users without specialized computing infrastructure, though you'll need API keys and associated costs for the LLM service calls during optimization.\n\nThe typical optimization loop uses 100–500 evaluations, which scales based on your evaluation metric complexity rather than GPU availability.","durationMs":4162,"url":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/gepa-ai/gepa/main/README.md"}}
